   L243: IntroductIon
>> L244: Energy poverty occurs when a household is unable to secure a level and
   L245: quality of domestic energy services—space cooling and heating, cooking,
   L246: appliances, information technology—sufficient for its social and material
>> L247: needs. This somewhat contested and broad definition lies at the tip of a vast
   L248: scientific and policy iceberg, involving complex socio-technical relations
>> L249: that extend across the planet. Energy poverty affects millions of people
   L250: worldwide, even if the causes and consequences vary depending on con-
   L251: text. Historically, the existence of this condition in the Global North has
