>> L525: Understanding Energy Poverty, Vulnerability
   L526: and Justice
>> L527: Abstract This chapter outlines past and current definitional issues at the
>> L528: nexus of energy poverty, energy vulnerability, energy justice and energy
   L529: transitions. It traces the historical development of scientific understand-
   L530: ings centring on these topics, while exploring their interactions and inter-
>> L531: dependencies. The chapter starts from the multiple definitional
>> L532: controversies surrounding fuel poverty and energy poverty, to then dis-
   L533: cuss the different ways in which notions of energy vulnerability and energy
   L534: justice have enriched traditional understandings. The latter has been
   L535: achieved, in part, thanks to a fuller appreciation of the services and pro-
   L536: duction chains via which energy circulates across territories.
>> L537: Keywords Energy poverty • Energy vulnerability • Energy justice • Energy
   L538: transitions • Energy services
