   L1729: CHAPTER 3
>> L1730: Energy Poverty Policies at the EU Level
   L1731: Abstract This chapter explores the historical evolution and present con-
>> L1732: tent of a common European Union (EU) energy poverty agenda. It iden-
   L1733: tifies the principal institutional and political drivers of this process, as well
   L1734: as the ways in which it has been translated into formal legal and policy
   L1735: documents. Also discussed are the key actors involved in promoting energy
   L1736: poverty-relevant policies, as well as recent trends in the development of a
   L1737: more coherent programme to address the difficulties faced by vulnerable
>> L1738: groups. The chapter argues that EU energy poverty policy has been lim-
   L1739: ited by the subsidiarity principle, and as such has been largely shaped by
   L1740: instruments related to the Single Market, even if energy efficiency and
   L1741: social policy-related efforts have also played a role.
>> L1742: Keywords Energy poverty • European Single Market • Policy subsidiarity
   L1743: • Energy transitions • European Union
   L1744: IntroductIon
>> L1745: This chapter provides an overview of how EU policy on energy poverty
   L1746: has emerged and developed over time. It details the content and struc-
   L1747: ture of relevant policy tools and legislation in the context of Europe’s
>> L1748: energy poverty-related infrastructural divide. In Bouzarovski and
   L1749: Petrova (2015b), we argued that in decision-maker and academic
