>> L2742: recession and social crisis has highlighted the relevance of energy poverty
   L2743: in Europe’s recovery and return to growth. The health community has
>> L2744: also been instrumental in forging the link between energy poverty and
   L2745: housing quality, supported by a coalition of stakeholders concerned with
   L2746: the quality of the housing stock and the implementation of the EED.
   L2747: Technology and climate change are two other strategic directions likely
>> L2748: to affect the direction of the EU energy poverty policy in the coming
   L2749: years. Smart metering—a growing priority of EU energy policy—holds
>> L2750: the potential to combat energy poverty in some instances, but its pros and
   L2751: cons for energy-poor users require careful consideration (Darby, 2012).
