   L2973: CHAPTER 4
   L2974: The European Energy Divide
   L2975: Abstract This chapter reviews the spatial and social differences that
>> L2976: underpin existing and past patterns of energy poverty in Europe. This is
   L2977: achieved via exploration of scientific research focused on the topic,
   L2978: either as a central object of enquiry or as part of wider investigations in
   L2979: which the issue is brought up as a relevant factor. Special attention is
>> L2980: paid to the large-scale geographic variation of energy poverty in Europe,
   L2981: as well as the manner in which this diversity is subsequently reflected at
   L2982: the level of nations, regions and particular demographic groups. I also
>> L2983: discuss the driving forces of energy poverty within particular spatial con-
   L2984: texts; and in an effort to move beyond the traditional geographic focus
>> L2985: of energy poverty research—the UK and Ireland—the chapter first sys-
   L2986: tematically overviews the development of a debate focusing on different
   L2987: parts of the European continent and its immediate neighbourhood. I
>> L2988: then review evidence about patterns of energy poverty at a variety of
   L2989: spatial scales.
