   L4112: Abstract This chapter summarizes the key findings of the book in the
   L4113: context of its purpose and frameworks, while recommending possible ave-
   L4114: nues for future research and policy.
>> L4115: Keywords Energy poverty • Energy vulnerability • Energy justice •
   L4116: European Union
   L4117: IntroductIon
   L4118: This book has explored the multiple layers of systemic change implicated
>> L4119: in the emergence of energy poverty in Europe and beyond. I have sought
   L4120: to highlight the embeddedness of vulnerability to domestic energy depri-
   L4121: vation in wider dynamics of organizational and social transformation. Of
   L4122: particular importance to this argument has been the need to understand
>> L4123: how energy poverty and vulnerability are both rooted in and arise out of
   L4124: the material and technical features that characterize the existence of an
   L4125: infrastructural divide in Europe. The divide operates at multiple levels and
   L4126: scales of activity—from the differences between nation states, to variations
   L4127: within the fabric of neighbourhoods and even households themselves. The
   L4128: divide itself can be seen as a socio-technical assemblage that is continu-
   L4129: ously dismantled and put together by multiple political interests and path
   L4130: dependencies. It is highly territorially contingent, which means that the
